  ▲ Unconditional recursion
   ╭─[test.lis:3:3]
 2 │ fn runs_forever(n: int) -> int {
 3 │   runs_forever(n - 1)
   ·   ─────────┬─────────
   ·            ╰── recurses on every path
 4 │ }
   ╰────
  help: `runs_forever` always calls itself, so it overflows the stack instead of returning. Add a base case that returns without recursing · code: [lint.unconditional_recursion]
